# Review routing. The last matching pattern wins, so the specific entries below
# the default are the ones that decide.
#
# @aj3x is the only maintainer today, so every line names the same person and
# nothing here gates anything yet. It is written anyway because the code is now
# 150 modules in fourteen features: when a second contributor arrives, the
# question "who should look at this?" has to have an answer that does not
# depend on recognising a path.
# The specific entries are not ceremony — each one is a place where a change
# that looks harmless, lints clean and leaves the suite green can still do real
# damage.

*                           @aj3x

# One line per place, so each feature can have its own owner. Today they are
# all the same person; when that changes, change the line, not the layout.
# What may import what is in eslint.config.js (BOUNDARIES), not here.
/src/app/                   @aj3x
/src/kernel/                @aj3x
/src/ui-kit/                @aj3x
/src/features/canvas/       @aj3x
/src/features/mode/         @aj3x
/src/features/walls/        @aj3x
/src/features/openings/     @aj3x
/src/features/room/         @aj3x
/src/features/furniture/    @aj3x
/src/features/floors/       @aj3x
/src/features/measure/      @aj3x
/src/features/walkpaths/    @aj3x
/src/features/layouts/      @aj3x
/src/features/library/      @aj3x
/src/features/marketplace/  @aj3x
/src/features/blueprint/    @aj3x

# Below this line, the entries that are not about who owns a feature but about
# what a harmless-looking change can break. They come last so they win.

# A feature's index.js is its public API: anything added here can be imported
# by every other feature, and anything removed can break one.
/src/features/*/index.js    @aj3x

# Saved-state shape and its migrations. migrate() runs on every load of every
# returning user's data; a wrong step here rewrites real projects with no error
# anywhere, and the damage is already on disk by the time anyone notices.
# S is also reassigned wholesale (setS), so its module is the one place the
# whole state object is defined.
/src/kernel/state.js        @aj3x
/src/kernel/migrate.js      @aj3x

# Every edit commits through transact(); a change here changes undo, saving and
# what repaints, everywhere at once.
/src/kernel/tx.js           @aj3x

# The 24 design tokens. They must stay CSS custom properties: dark mode works
# by re-declaring them under @media (prefers-color-scheme:dark), so converting
# one to a Sass $variable silently deletes dark mode with every test green.
/src/app/styles/_tokens.scss @aj3x

# Import/export is the only path a user's data leaves and re-enters the app by,
# and the collision rules decide whether a merge keeps or overwrites their work.
/src/features/io/           @aj3x

# The boundary rule and the cycle check. Loosening either lets features grow
# back into one another without a test going red.
/eslint.config.js           @aj3x
/scripts/import-cycles.mjs  @aj3x

# CI, Pages deployment and this file. A bad change here can publish the wrong
# thing to the live site, or quietly stop running the gate.
/.github/                   @aj3x

# The suite is capped at 20% of the codebase (ideally under 10%; it is at 12%
# of the app). Additions need an argument about what they catch, and deletions
# need to be distinguished from removing scaffolding that has finished its job
# — both are review questions, not mechanical ones. See test/README.md.
/test/                      @aj3x

# The build is what makes the one-file deployment model work: the include
# plugin, the classic script tag and the singlefile inlining are load-bearing.
/vite.config.js             @aj3x
